<h2 id=3D"stable-sorting">Stable Sorting</h2>
<p>Merge sort is a stable sorting algorithm. This is important in scenarios=
 where the original order of equal elements must be preserved. For example,=
 if we are sorting a list of nodes that share the same value, but have an a=
dditional attribute storing the time they were created, then it=E2=80=99s i=
mportant for the relative order of these nodes to stay the same. Stability =
can be important for database systems; for instance, where stable sorting i=
s required to maintain data integrity and consistency across multiple opera=
tions.</p><div class=3D"style_markCompleteWrap__YEi4w"><button class=3D"sty=
